course: dictionary
lesson: 6532
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Netting is a noun for material made of string, rope, wire or plastic threads tied or woven into a mesh with holes. «Loose garden netting can trap birds and hedgehogs, so it is kept tight or taken away.» Here netting is the material over the vegetables, and the holes are what catch the animals.
explain: Netting also comes from the verb net. To net something can mean to catch it in a net, to score a goal, or to earn money after costs. Read the words around it first: if they are about a net, a goal or money, that meaning may fit.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Loose garden netting tangles birds and hedgehogs» makes sense with the noun, because a loose net can catch them. Always ask: does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Netting is made of string, rope, wire or plastic threads woven into a mesh with holes.
fact: Gardeners use bird netting to protect fruit and vegetables from birds.
fact: Safety netting and trampoline netting are used to stop people falling.
fact: «Loose garden netting can trap birds and hedgehogs, so it is kept tight or taken away.»
fact: As a verb, net can mean to catch something, to score a goal, or to earn money after costs.
exercise: «Loose garden netting can trap birds and hedgehogs.» In this sentence, what is netting? | A small animal that lives in gardens | *A material made of threads tied into a mesh with holes | A goal kicked into the net | A type of fast running shoe
exercise: A striker says, «I netted twice in the second half.» What does netted mean? | *Scored a goal | Lost the ball | Caught a fish in a net | Wrapped something up in string
exercise: What is safety netting used for? | To make a shirt warm | *To stop people falling | To cook fish over a fire | To grow tomatoes
test: «The shop netted £200 after paying its costs.» What does netted mean here? | Dropped on the floor | Lost, because of the costs | Counted twice | *Earned, once the costs were paid
test: «Trampoline netting stops falls.» What job does the netting do? | It makes the trampoline bounce higher | It holds the trampoline up | *It keeps people from falling off | It keeps the rain out
exam: The fisherman «netted a big fish» before lunch. What does netted mean here? | Thrown back into the sea | Cooked on a stove | *Caught in a net | Measured with a ruler
